,"name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"American (New), Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"TzkVUJab9Sh0CqDk2sCF-w","review_id":"BYDPopb79KH-aMt3do3Mjg","date":"2008-01-21T17:32:03","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9556288123130798,"text_excerpt":"I was so happy to finally go to Bayona, I've been wanting to for years and as a local it's a shame I hadn't been before. It was very very good and very cozy and relaxing, very New Orleans. I don't know why other reviewers thought it stuffy, we wore jeans. First though, why didn't I give it five stars? Because the service was just a hair below excellent and what I would have expected. Bad night? Probably. It's not that I wouldn't go again. Just a few little glitches. Normally I don't mind sitting at the dinner table for three hours with friends, but we missed the parade for crimony sakes. I'm guessing this was unusual. Now the good part. While Bayona does seem to be a shrine to duck fat an..."},{"business_id":"TzkVUJab9Sh0CqDk2sCF-w","review_id":"CHo2hroCAy6rymCYbepXxA","date":"2016-04-01T15:08:13","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9430316686630249,"text_excerpt":"This was the nicest meal we had on our recent trip to NO. We had heard good things and wanted to give it a try. Better make your reservation early. We called for our reservation early on a Tuesday and 8:30 was the earliest we could get in. From what I hear, we were luck to get in on the same day! Bayona is located is a neat little building with the entrance on the side. Décor is rather traditional. It's small, with seating for 50-60 at a time. Tables were situated a little too close for my liking. We were early and waited in their small waiting area with seating for about 12. I would rate the wait staff at 4 stars, only because they were hard pressed to keep up with the crowded room. The ..."},{"business_id":"TzkVUJab9Sh0CqDk2sCF-w","review_id":"ro6-N13PhS41HS4xjeH__Q","date":"2018-07-26T18:44:15","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.941682755947113,"text_excerpt":"How is it that I'm a native and have never, in it's almost 30 years, been to Bayona? Well, all of that changed last Friday when I enjoyed one of the best meals I have had in this city that I so love. First off, Bayona is housed in an adorable creole cottage, tucked away into a quiet block of the French Quarter, yet only a block away from Bourbon Street. It's like a little oasis amid all the madness. Upon entering, we were enthusiastically greeted by a most friendly and energetic host. She quickly walked us to their \"best table,\" which was perfect. We were in the dining room closest to the street but also offered a glimpse of the entrance which is a walkway down the side of the building. I..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"TzkVUJab9Sh0CqDk2sCF-w","photo_id":"FC80ZaZu2E_FPddi0s5AuA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/FC80ZaZu2E_FPddi0s5AuA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8649893403053284},{"business_id":"TzkVUJab9Sh0CqDk2sCF-w","photo_id":"_adT3VPuil24-Dnr4sLLLA","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/_adT3VPuil24-Dnr4s